# V build artifacts
# Anchored: bare `blobly_net` matches at EVERY depth, including the cmd/blobly_net SOURCE
# directory — which silently swallowed all 19 files of the #123 split while the commit deleted
# their lines from main.v, and had already eaten a source dir once before (the memory that names
# this pattern). The in-directory binary is covered by the cmd/blobly_net/blobly_net line below.
/blobly_net
/main
cmd/mf4_dump/mf4_dump
*.tmp.c
/src/main
/src/blobly_net
/build/
# compiled binaries left next to sources by `v run` / `-o` (Windows .exe, bare on Linux)
*.exe
cmd/blobly_net/blobly_net
cmd/blobly_net/main

# Editor
*.swp

# Python tools venv (asammdf MF4 bridge) — dev-only, not committed
.venv-tools/
# Python DoIP oracle venv (scapy) — dev-only, not committed
.venv-doip/

# Private external DBCs copied in locally for simulation — NOT ours to commit.
dbc/ecu_vcm/
projects/ecu-vcm.yml

# MF4 recordings are private/binary — never commit one anywhere in the tree
# (the only exception is the tiny synthetic samples/demo.mf4, re-included below).
*.mf4
# Real MF4 sample recordings (binary, fetched by scripts/setup_mf4_tools.sh).
# Exclude the contents but not the dir itself, so the demo log below can be
# re-included (git can't un-ignore a file whose parent dir is excluded).
samples/*
# …but ship the tiny candump demo log + its MF4 twin so "Open Log" (and the
# MF4-aware open) work out of the box, plus the 8 KB two-bus fixture: a
# single-bus file cannot catch a reader that merges buses (#90).
!samples/demo.log
!samples/demo.mf4
!samples/two_buses.mf4
!samples/both_dirs.mf4

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
heaptrack.*.gz
massif.out.*
imgui.ini
# Captures from the Record button: timestamped (recording-YYYYMMDD-HHmmss[-N].log), written
# beside the open project — which for the shipped example projects is inside this repo.
# DELIBERATELY unanchored, unlike the source-dir patterns above: these names are generated,
# collide with no directory, and must be caught at any depth a project lives at.
recording-*.log

# Agent working state — sessions, worktrees, scratch. Never published: a stray
# `git add -A` would otherwise sweep transcripts and worktree checkouts into the repo.
.claude/

# GUI dependency evaluation tree — vendored C sources + their build objects, fetched
# by scripts, rebuilt on demand. Not ours to ship and not reproducible from git alone.
eval/

# Personal editor task wiring: paths are machine-specific (local MSYS2 install), so it
# is kept out of the repo. .vscode/launch.json IS shared — it uses ${workspaceFolder} only.
.vscode/tasks.json

